stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> OPEN: TK1 raised by a machine event, a validator or a person, with a named holder and a due moment
    OPEN --> WAITING: TK2 the act passes to someone outside the product - an employee, an authority, a counterparty
    WAITING --> OPEN: TK3 the awaited fact arrives and is recorded
    OPEN --> BLOCKED: TK4 a precondition the holder cannot clear
    BLOCKED --> OPEN: TK5 the blocker clears, with its evidence
    OPEN --> DONE: TK6 closure evidence recorded
    WAITING --> DONE: TK7 the awaited artefact itself is the closure evidence
    OPEN --> WAIVED: TK8 waivable class only, typed reason, named waiver, one period
    OPEN --> VOID: TK9 the obligation ceases before the act is owed
    WAITING --> VOID: TK9 the obligation ceases before the act is owed
    BLOCKED --> VOID: TK9 the obligation ceases before the act is owed
    OPEN --> SUPERSEDED: TK10 re-raised on a new subject, holder or period
    WAITING --> SUPERSEDED: TK10 re-raised on a new subject, holder or period
    BLOCKED --> SUPERSEDED: TK10 re-raised on a new subject, holder or period
    DONE --> [*]
    WAIVED --> [*]
    VOID --> [*]
    SUPERSEDED --> [*]

    note right of OPEN
        A holder is always a named person, never a role with no holder
        Re-derived on a role change - never reassigned to the maker
        Escalation finds a second person, never a waiver
    end note

    note right of BLOCKED
        The blocker and its owner are on the face of the item
        A blocked item is still visible and still counted
        A due date passing never closes an item
    end note

    note right of DONE
        Terminal - a closed item is never reopened
        A recurrence is a new item linked to this one
    end note
